**Cause**: `depth` has no base case: when a node has no children it recurses on the same node forever until the call stack overflows.

**Fix**:
```js
function depth(node) {
  if (!node.children.length) return 1;
  return 1 + Math.max(...node.children.map(depth));
}
```
Recursion must stop on leaf nodes.

**Prevent**: Write the base case first, and test recursive functions on the smallest input.

